course: dictionary
lesson: 11948
title: Carbonation and fizzy drinks
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Carbonation is the fizz in a drink. It happens when carbon dioxide gas is added to a drink, so bubbles form. «The lemonade had lots of carbonation, so it sparkled in the glass.» Here carbonation means the fizziness the gas gives the drink.
explain: Pressure squeezes the gas into the liquid. When you open the bottle, the pressure drops and the gas escapes as bubbles. «Shake the bottle and it sprays everywhere» because the gas escapes quickly. The carbonation is what makes it spray.
explain: The word also has a science meaning: a chemical reaction with carbon dioxide. «Limestone can change when it reacts with carbon dioxide.» Look at the words around it. If the sentence is about a drink, carbonation means fizz. If it is about rock or chemicals, it means the reaction.
fact: Carbonation means adding carbon dioxide gas to a drink so it becomes fizzy.
fact: Carbonation also means the fizziness of a drink itself.
fact: «Flat» lemonade has lost its carbonation, so it has no fizz left.
fact: Carbon dioxide is a gas we breathe out, and its short name is CO2.
fact: In science, carbonation can mean a reaction with carbon dioxide, such as when limestone or concrete reacts with it.
exercise: «The drink had plenty of carbonation.» What does carbonation mean here? | The sweetness of the drink | The cold temperature of the drink | *The fizziness of the drink | The colour of the drink
exercise: Why does a shaken bottle spray when it is opened? | Because the bottle is empty | Because the drink is too cold | *Because the gas escapes fast | Because the lid is too tight
exercise: Which drink has lost its carbonation? | Fizzy cola | *Flat lemonade | Sparkling mineral water | Freshly opened soda
test: What is carbonation in a fizzy drink? | Sugar that makes it sweet | Colouring that makes it bright | Ice that makes it cold | *Carbon dioxide gas that makes it fizzy
test: Which sentence uses carbonation as a science word? | Pour the carbonation into the cup | Carbonation makes the drink fizzy | The bottle has lots of carbonation | *Limestone and carbon dioxide react, a process called carbonation
exam: Why does a bottle of fizzy drink go flat if it is left open for a day? | The drink gets heavier | The bottle shrinks | The sugar turns into water | *The carbonation escapes into the air
